//! An app and the pipeline that builds and runs it, in three stages: an [`App`] (the
//! definition), a [`Built`] (the artifacts per target) and a [`Running`] (live processes).
//! Each step is scoped under the stage it takes, so `App.build` takes an App and gives a
//! Built, and `Built.launch` takes a Built and gives a Running. Steps are effects, so a chain
//! starts with `run`:
//!
//! ```silk,ignore
//! effect fn app() -> App {
//!   return run App.make("my-app")
//!     |> App.framework(Framework.react("."))
//!     |> App.target(Target.window(Window { title: "My app", width: 900.0, height: 600.0 }))
//! }
//!
//! // The app draws under the window's title bar on macOS, and a press in its top 56 pixels
//! // moves the window.
//! Target.window(Window { title: "My app", width: 900.0, height: 600.0 })
//!   .titleBar(TitleBar.transparent(56.0))
//!
//! // The same, with the window buttons 20 pixels from the left and 18 from the top.
//!   .titleBar(TitleBar.transparent(56.0).buttons(20.0, 18.0))
//!
//! // The Metal Performance HUD over the window on macOS: presented fps and frame times.
//!   .metalHud(true)
//!
//! run app() |> App.only(target) |> App.dev(&options) |> Built.launch() |> Running.watch()
//! run app() |> App.only(target) |> App.build(&options) |> Built.write("dist")
//! ```
//!
//! A project's own step is a function of the same shape, `effect fn sign<'env, E, ?R>(built:
//! once Effect<'env; Built ! E ? R>) -> Built ! … ? …`, placed in the chain. `tap` and `map`
//! take a closure for something small between two steps.
//!
//! The steps run inside a task (`silk task`): they use the task's root as the project
//! directory and its compiler for `silk build`.
import stylesheets
import host { Kind, Plan, main as hostMain, page as hostPage, webgpuExports, libm }
import manifest { Project, read as readProject }
